From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:23:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 576/576] media: i2c: hi556: LOCAL: mirror the front camera by
 default

The owner wants the built-in front camera to behave like a mirror unless userspace
says otherwise. This is policy, so it stays in this series, and upstream keeps the
default of 0. Frames saved or sent are mirrored too.
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
index 6a9c0df49..65e2de445 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi556.c
@@ -934,7 +934,7 @@ static int hi556_init_controls(struct hi556 *hi556)
 						HI556_DGTL_GAIN_MIN, HI556_DGTL_GAIN_MAX,
 						HI556_DGTL_GAIN_STEP,
 						HI556_DGTL_GAIN_DEFAULT);
-	hi556->hflip = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(ctrl_hdlr, &hi556_ctrl_ops, V4L2_CID_HFLIP, 0, 1, 1, 0);
+	hi556->hflip = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(ctrl_hdlr, &hi556_ctrl_ops, V4L2_CID_HFLIP, 0, 1, 1, 1);
 	if (hi556->hflip)
 		hi556->hflip->flags |= V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_MODIFY_LAYOUT;
 	/* 256 is unity, as for the digital gain, which they multiply. */
